    ^{:line 88 :tag bool :doc "A prefixed instruction is generated by this opcode. This cannot be placed\nacross a 64B PC address. Opcodes should not translate to more than one\nprefixed instruction. The prefixed instruction should be written first\n(e.g when Optab.size > 8).\n"} ispfx

    ^{:line 90 :tag (func [(* ctxt9) (* obj/Prog) (* Optab) (* (array 5 uint32))])} asmout))


















(go/var ^{:tag (slice Optab) :doc "optab contains an array to be sliced of accepted operand combinations for an\ninstruction. Unused arguments and fields are not explicitly enumerated, and\nshould not be listed for clarity. Unused arguments and values should always\nassume the default value for the given type.\n\noptab does not list every valid ppc64 opcode, it enumerates representative\noperand combinations for a class of instruction.  The variable oprange indexes\nall valid ppc64 opcodes.\n\noprange is initialized to point a slice within optab which contains the valid\noperand combinations for a given instruction.  This is initialized from buildop.\n\nLikewise, each slice of optab is dynamically sorted using the ocmp Sort interface\nto arrange entries to minimize text size of each opcode.\n\noptab is the sorted result of combining optabBase, optabGen, and prefixableOptab.\n"} optab)

